  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Scattered showers and thunderstorms later this \nafternoon and evening. Still a chance for gusty winds and heavy\ndownpours with localized flash flooding possible.\n\nTiming of showers and storms over Ohio will be such that much\nof central PA will not a lot of time to heat up today. ALso the\nairmass over much of the area has been worked over the last \nfew days, and lower dewpoints are in place. Thus expect less\ncoverage than on Friday. The one area that still has the higher\ndewpoints is across the southeast. This area will have the \nbetter chance to heat up today as well. Not a lot of shear,\nbut CAPE is still up there. \n\nSunday looks like a break from the showers and storms, but with\nthe advection of more humid and hot air again from the western\nstates, and weak shortwaves moving along in a fairly fast \nwest to east jet stream, showers and storms will be back in\nthe area after Sunday again. The current pattern likely to \nhold for much of next week, before a cool down late week.",
